      "body": "**Title: Fix Xid 31 MMU fault in EP16 CUDA-graph replay (reduce_scatterv)**\r\n\r\n**Description**: Fixes #59607.\r\n\r\n**Bug:** During CUDA graph capture (e.g., EP16 piecewise mode), pynccl.reduce_scatterv and all_gatherv bake Python-computed slice addresses (data_ptr) directly into the graph. On replay, if per-rank batch distributions change, these hardcoded pointers become stale and point to invalid memory, triggering Xid 31 MMU faults.\r\n\r\n**Fix:**\r\n\r\nImplemented a graph-safe fallback in cuda_communicator.py when heterogeneous sizes are detected during graph capture.\r\nThe fallback pads the inputs to the maximum size and uses uniform ncclReduceScatter/ncclAllGather (which have fixed/stable tensor addresses), safely slicing the padding away afterward.\r\nAdded safety warnings in pynccl.py to catch any future usage that might accidentally bake stale pointers into CUDA graphs.",
